message.content:
This is a card-and-dice game sold as a set, so it falls in heading 9504 (articles for arcade, table or parlor games). Playing cards of heading 9504.40 are limited to standard playing cards, and this set contains custom game cards and dice, so it does not fit there. The best fit is the "other" subheading 9504.90, which covers table games. I recall the 9504.90.80 line as "Other" with the 9504.90.8000 statistical suffix, but I haven't verified that against the current schedule.

The set is a board-less game made of cards and dice, so 9504.90.6000 (tables games and parlor games other than board games) is also a candidate. In 9504.90, the 9504.90.40 line covers game board sets such as chess and checkers, and 9504.90.60 covers "Other". That would make 9504.90.6000 the likelier code for a drinking game of cards and dice. CBP rulings on similar card games, such as "Cards Against Humanity", have used 9504.90.6000, so I'm going with that.

{"hts_code": "9504.90.6000", "reason": "The adult drinking game, made up of dice and specialized game cards, is a parlor/table game of heading 9504 that falls under the 'other' articles for parlor games in subheading 9504.90.60."}
